GUI modernization, Phase 1: the app-shell/sidebar scroll fix (ADR 0003),
closing P0-01, P1-03, P1-04, P1-10.

## 1. The fix

`.app-shell` (renamed `.app-frame`) now bounds itself to `block-size: 100dvh`
with `overflow: hidden` instead of only `min-height: 100vh`. `.sidebar`
became its own three-row grid (header / scrollable nav / footer) instead of
one flex column with `margin-top: auto` pushing the language toggle down -
a technique that only worked while the sidebar's height matched the
viewport, which stopped being true the moment page content grew past it.
`.main` became `.workspace-header` (sticky) + `.workspace-body` (the one
normal scroll region). `Sidebar.tsx`'s nav items became native `<button>`s
inside a labelled `<nav>`, replacing `<div role="button" tabIndex={0}>` and
its hand-rolled Enter/Space handling.

