## 3. Manual visual verification (Browser pane, real rendering, not just
assertions)

Timeline page, 900x600, English, dark mode (this machine's OS theme):
scrolled to the bottom of 44 unvirtualized events (event timestamps
22:21:2x, well past the 22:20:17 start) - the sidebar, all eight nav
buttons, and "NetRewind" stayed exactly in place throughout, confirmed by
reading `.lang-toggle`'s live `getBoundingClientRect()` in the browser
console after scrolling: `{top: 559.33, bottom: 588.00}` inside a 600px
viewport - independent confirmation of what the Playwright suite already
asserts, from a second code path (manual DevTools-style inspection, not the
test harness).

Wizard privacy step (the longest of the six), 720x480, Arabic: full title,
subtitle, and body paragraph rendered with no clipping, and all three
actions (تخطّ الآن / السابق / التالي) visible without scrolling - compared
directly against the same step before the fix, which needed to scroll past
the fold to reach any action button.

## 4. A defect found outside the original scope, fixed along the way

`.wizard-overlay`/`.wizard-card` had the identical defect class
(`min-height: 100vh`, no bound, no internal scroll region) - not called out
by name in the execution order's phase list, but the same root cause and
the same fix pattern this phase was already building. Measured before the
fix: the privacy step overflowed a 720x480 window by 15px
(`document.documentElement.scrollHeight = 495` vs. `clientHeight = 480`) -
small, but real, and the product release plan explicitly asks for the
wizard's action buttons to stay reachable without scrolling at a short
window. Fixed with the same containment technique (`Wizard.tsx` gained a
`.wizard-step-body` wrapper so `.wizard-card` can pin its progress dots and
action bar while only the step content scrolls). Regression test:
`desktop/tests/visual/wizard-layout.spec.ts`.

## 5. Deliberately deferred, and why

- Icon-based sidebar rail collapse at 720-899px width (per the execution
  order's §4.1) needs an icon system that does not exist until Phase 2's
  component library. For now, the sidebar narrows its text column
  (`--nav-width: 180px` under 900px) instead - verified in the matrix down
  to 720px wide with no label clipping or overflow, so nothing is broken
  while the icon-rail treatment waits for the right phase.
- A fully separated `WorkspaceHeader` component (with a time-range picker,
  filters, etc.) is not built yet - today's `.workspace-header` holds only
  `SourceBanner`, because page title/subtitle markup still lives inside
  each page component rather than a shared header. That extraction belongs
  with Phase 3's `InvestigationContext` work, where a real shared header
  first has something besides the banner to hold.
- Manual theme (high-contrast, reduced-transparency) is Phase 2 scope; only
  OS-level light/dark (`prefers-color-scheme`, already implemented) was
  tested this phase.
